[?2004l[?2004h> p.write_text(s)
[?2004l[?2004h> p = Path('tests/test_multi_currency.py')
[?2004l[?2004h> s = p.read_text().replace('    a = open_account(conn, "1000", "Cash", "asset", "2026-01-01")', '    open_account(conn, "1000", "Cash", "asset", "2026-01-01")')
[?2004l[?2004h> p.write_text(s)
[?2004l[?2004h> p = Path('README.md')
[?2004l[?2004h> s = p.read_text().replace('python -m ledger post CODE AMOUNT_CENTS DATE', 'python -m ledger post CODE AMOUNT_CENTS DATE [--currency CCC]').replace('--reason R --approved-by U', '--reason R --approved-by U [--currency CCC]')
[?2004l[?2004h> s += '''
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Multi-currency (FIN-311)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Accounts have a single currency (three upper-case ASCII letters), defaulting to
[?2004l[?2004h> USD. Open EUR accounts through the Python API:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```python
[?2004l[?2004h> from ledger import accounts, db
[?2004l[?2004h> conn = db.connect()
[?2004l[?2004h> account = accounts.open_account(conn, "EU-1000", "EU Cash", "asset", "2026-12-01", currency="EUR")
[?2004l[?2004h> conn.close()
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Amounts remain integer minor units; the ledger does not perform FX conversion.
[?2004l[?2004h> `post_entry` and `post_adjustment` accept `currency=None` (use the account currency)
[?2004l[?2004h> or an explicit matching currency. A mismatch raises `PostingError` without posting.
[?2004l[?2004h> The CLI exposes the same choice via `--currency`. Reports label each account's
[?2004l[?2004h> currency and print separate trial balances. `reports.trial_balance()` now returns
[?2004l[?2004h> `{currency: {"debits": ..., "credits": ..., "difference": ...}}`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Migration `0007` defaults all existing accounts and entries to USD and preserves
[?2004l[?2004h> adjustments and retained history unchanged. Back up the database before rollout.
[?2004l[?2004h> Retention intentionally leaves references to archived accounts; the adjustments
[?2004l[?2004h> rebuild uses `fk_mode="defer"` to carry these through, and recreates its index.
[?2004l[?2004h> Do not prune these references: they are financial history, not disposable rows.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''
[?2004l[?2004h> p.write_text(s)
[?2004l[?2004h> PY
